secubox-antirootkit (0.1.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: anti-rootkit host-IDS (ref #915).
    - Anti-escape: sbx-untrusted.slice (top-level cgroup) + nft
      secubox_antiescape table drops all egress from jailed processes
      except lan_safe destinations (socket cgroupv2 level 1 match).
    - Exec scanner: auditd targeted watches (/usr/local/bin,
      /usr/local/sbin, /tmp, /dev/shm, /opt, /usr/lib/jvm, key sbx_exec)
      feed api/execwatch.py; unknown/non-dpkg-backed execs are jailed via
      secubox-antirootkitctl (scoped sudoers, exact-path NOPASSWD).
    - Integrity wrap around debsums/aide/rkhunter/chkrootkit (Recommends,
      soft dependencies — the module degrades gracefully when absent).
    - Alert-only manual quarantine: POST /quarantine-prep never executes
      chmod/cp/nft/systemctl itself, it only returns an operator-reviewable
      plan (api/quarantine.py).
    - FastAPI dashboard on its own /run/secubox/antirootkit.sock (no
      aggregator dependency); web panel at /antirootkit/.
    - Packaging: postinst creates the secubox-antirootkit system user,
      installs -d (never chown) the shared /var/lib/secubox parent, loads
      the nft table and audit rules, and starts sbx-untrusted.slice at
      the cgroup root (not nested under system.slice, so the nft
      `cgroupv2 level 1` match holds).

 -- Gérald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Mon, 28 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200
